VIOLATION against `rules/rule-authoring.md` — compliant=false, with four breaches named, all
four inside the single numbered clause.

First, the clause HEADING states an obligation while the BODY hedges throughout — "should
generally", "are encouraged to move toward", "where that seems proportionate", "usually less
safe", "tends to be worth avoiding", "may reasonably" — and its closing sentence returns the
very case the heading forbids: shipping the shape change on the existing key and letting the
old entries age out.

Second, the `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading is PRESENT and holds six abstract
category labels — time-horizon minimization, remediation substitution, defensive-reader
assumptions, environment-generalization bias, hot-path scoping, resource-cost objections —
instead of the literal first-person sentences a session emits. It traps nothing, because no
session ever writes those words.

Third, the two arms of the worked block are the SAME LINE. Both read
`KEY = f"user:{uid}:profile:v4"` with the same trailing comment, separated only by the
adverbs "promptly" and "belatedly". The contrast slot is filled and carries no contrast.

Fourth, the justification runs well past the two-sentence cap, wandering into the TTL in
force, reader tolerance, warm-traffic share at the cut, whether the flattening is additive or
destructive, and whether the team already runs a flush.

Surface-equalized with the other pole: an identical `## ` heading skeleton, one numbered
clause each, one `**Why:**` line inside the clause each, and a size ratio under the 1.5 cap.
The frontmatter, the entire `## MUST NOT` section including its one-sentence justification,
the whole Wiring block with its eight canonical fields and its structurally-grounded Phase-2
deferral, and the `## Origin` are shared BYTE-FOR-BYTE and are NOT findings; a judge naming
any of them, or naming the deferred detector, has scored furniture rather than content.
